  "intro": {
    "title": "Fahren, not gehen",
    "paragraphs": [
      "German separates going on foot (gehen) from going by vehicle (fahren). If there's a car, bus, train, bike or boat involved, it's fahren. Ich fahre nach Berlin: I'm going to Berlin (by train or car)."
    ]
  },
